<title>SWEDEN: Swedish unions welcome PM's cash pledge.</title>
<headline>Swedish unions welcome PM's cash pledge.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's main trade union body, LO, said on Thursday it welcomed Prime Minister Goran Persson's pledge to give more money to health care, the elderly and education.</p>
<p>&quot;Hopefully, this also means that the debate on paying off state debt before unemployment is slashed is over,&quot; LO deputy head Wanja Lundby-Wedin said in a statement.</p>
<p>She said Persson's pledge in parliament on Wednesday to use a 10-billion crown budget surplus in 1998 on welfare spending met union demands for higher spending.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
